  "id": "dual-action-antidepressant",
  "term": "dual-action antidepressant",
  "definition": "A dual-action antidepressant is an antidepressant described here as working on several pathways in the brain rather than just one. In this source, venlafaxine is given as an example and is said to affect brain areas linked with heightened anxiety and hyper-arousal in post-traumatic stress disorder.",
